<h2>How it works</h2>

<p>Delegates create a profile stating what they sell or want to buy, then
request meetings with other delegates. The Secretariat schedules every accepted
meeting into a Day 2 slot.</p>

<h2>Writing a profile that works</h2>

<p>The Secretariat reads every profile and books the meetings by hand. A
profile that states what an organisation trades, in what volume and what it is
looking for gets more meetings than one describing the organisation in general
terms.</p>

<p>Useful detail: product and grade, annual volume, target markets, current
certifications, and the specific counterpart being sought.</p>

<h2>Who takes part</h2>

<ul class="classes">
  <li class="class-row"><span class="class-row__name">Producers and processors</span><p>Meeting importers, distributors and consumer brands.</p></li>
  <li class="class-row"><span class="class-row__name">Buyers and importers</span><p>Meeting exporters with the grades and volumes they need.</p></li>
  <li class="class-row"><span class="class-row__name">Machinery and technology suppliers</span><p>Meeting factories planning capacity or upgrades.</p></li>
  <li class="class-row"><span class="class-row__name">Investors and financiers</span><p>Meeting operators with projects across the value chain.</p></li>
</ul>

<h2>Get access</h2>

<p>B2B meetings run through the delegate portal. Register first, and the
Secretariat opens profiles when they go live.</p>
